      "id": "new-from-cog",
      "name": "Field Boundaries (STAC)",
      "isActive": true,
      "data": [
        {
          "url": "https://eoresults.esa.int/stac/collections/delineate-anything-field-boundaries-2025/items?limit=500",
          "format": "stac",
          "zIndex": 50,
          "style": [
            {
              "stroke-color": "#3b82f6",
              "stroke-width": 2,
              "_name": "Solid line"
            }
          ],
          "minZoom": 11,
          "maxZoom": 20,
          "assets": [
            "data"
          ],
          "assetFormats": {
            "data": "flatgeobuf"
          }
        }
      ],
      "meta": {
        "description": "### Description\nThis interactive map shows field boundaries for 103 countries generated with the **Delineate Anything v2** algorithm applied to the 2025 Sentinel-2 Global Mosaics (S2GM), with the WorldCereal 2021 map used as a delineation mask. \n\nZoom in to any footprint area.  Field boundaries appear when  scalebar reads **5 km or less**.\n\n*Please note*: field boundaries are overlaid on high-resolution satellite imagery from the Stadia Maps service. As a result, some misalignment may be visible, since the boundaries were derived from Sentinel-2 data.\n\n### Further information\nDetails of methodology are available on the [Delineate Anything Project Page](https://lavreniuk.github.io/Delineate-Anything/)\n\n### Download\nField boundaries are available for download as flatgeobuff  files with named suffixes ISO 3166 [two country letter codes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-1_alpha-2):\n\n[**Download >>>**](https://eoresults.esa.int/d/delineate-anything-field-boundaries-2025/2025/01/01/)\n\n### Authors\n[Mykola Lavreniuk](https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=-oFR-RYAAAAJ) (1,2), [Nataliia Kussul](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=e3TWBuwAAAAJ&hl=en) (3), [Andrii Shelestov](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=tqoQKZAAAAAJ&hl=en) (2,4), [Bohdan Yailymov](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=XaN-oukAAAAJ&hl=en) (2), [Yevhenii Salii](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=4jgAsBIAAAAJ&hl=en) (2,4), [Volodymyr Kuzin](https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Volodymyr-Kuzin) (2,4), [Zoltan Szantoi](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=P_pyhi8AAAAJ&hl=en) (1)\n\n[1] European Space Agency, [2] SRI NASU-SSAU, [3] University of Maryland, [4] Igor Sikorsky Kyiv Polytechnic Institute",
        "attribution": {
          "text": "Data attribution not specified"
        },
